# CVE-2026-14456: OpenSSL QUIC server unbounded memory allocation via unlimited pending
# connections (DoS) — Packages: libcrypto3 3.5.7-r0 and libssl3 3.5.7-r0 in Alpine base image
# Severity: HIGH — advisory published 2026-08-13 (https://openssl-library.org/news/secadv/20260813.txt)
# No upstream fix available: Alpine's v3.24 branch still ships libcrypto3/libssl3 3.5.7-r0
# (build date 2026-06-10, before the advisory). OpenSSL's QUIC SERVER implementation allocates
# and queues new incoming channels with no limit when processing valid Initial packets for
# unknown destination connection IDs, letting a remote peer grow memory unboundedly and make the
# QUIC listener unavailable. Affects OpenSSL 3.5+; upstream fix caps pending connections at 256.
# Charon's Caddy HTTP/3 stack uses github.com/quic-go/quic-go (pure Go, userspace QUIC) — no
# OpenSSL-based QUIC server is ever run. libcrypto3/libssl3 are present only as Alpine system
# libraries backing TLS-client tools (wget/curl/busybox-extras); the vulnerable QUIC server code
# path is never invoked in this deployment.
# Review by: 2026-11-19
# See also: .grype.yaml for full justification
# exp: 2026-11-19
CVE-2026-14456

